====================================================================================================
ASSEMBLY: L(S) = R' * meas(R-safe) * meas(Q-lonely) >= R' * meas(R-safe) * c_r
====================================================================================================
   The minorant CLOSES the apex factor: meas(Q-lonely) >= c_r > 0 uniformly (r=2..6).
   c_r:  c_2=0.7253, c_3=0.6044, c_4=0.4943, c_5=0.3815, c_6=0.2810
   So L(S) > 0  <==  R' * meas(R-safe) > 0, i.e. the OPEN content is exactly the COUPLING
   R' >= c (Node-3) and the R-safe measure floor (the 14-free wide part).
   The apex/few-apex block -- the NEW structure of the r=2..6 case -- is uniformly handled.

DONE.
